- validator.getKeyword() could return null -> equals comparison with string works fine (null.equals? Actually "unevaluatedProperties".equals(null) returns false, no NPE). So safe.
- validator.getKeyword() could throw runtime exception (unlikely but possible). Not typical.

Thus exception scenarios: parent schema null, validators list null, validator null element.

